# V-221 — Cloudflare Pages cache headers for the marketing site.
#
# Strategy in detail at docs/deployment/cdn-strategy.md.
# Three tiers:
#   1. Hashed assets (immutable, 1y)        — /_astro/*, fonts, images
#   2. Marketing pages (medium, 5m / 1d edge) — html
#   3. Crawler artefacts (1h)                — robots.txt, sitemaps
#
# Cloudflare Pages copies public/_headers verbatim into the deploy and
# applies these per-path. ⚠️ ALL matching rules apply and later/broad
# matches MERGE onto earlier ones (there is no first-match-wins) — so
# the `/*` catch-all must never set Cache-Control. More-
# specific patterns above broader ones.
#
# Format reference:
#   https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/

# ── Hashed Astro bundles + CSS ───────────────────────────────────────
# Astro emits hashed filenames under /_astro/* — the hash flips on
# every content change so customers always re-fetch on real updates;
# in between, the browser + edge cache the file forever.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# ── Static media (images, fonts) ─────────────────────────────────────
# Hash-versioned via Astro pipeline OR uploaded with stable names; in
# either case treat as immutable. If a stable-name image needs to
# change, deploy with a new filename (or add a query string).
/*.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.jpg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.jpeg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.webp
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.avif
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.ico
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.woff
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.woff2
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# ── Self-hosted fonts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Geist (variable) + JetBrains Mono, vendored under public/fonts/ with
# their OFL.txt licenses. Needed EXPLICITLY: CF Pages /*.woff2 globs do
# NOT match nested paths in production (measured max-age=14400 on
# /fonts/** 2026-07-04 — Lighthouse flagged the ~180 KiB re-download).
# Filenames are unversioned but the binaries only change on an
# intentional font upgrade — treat as immutable. Mirrors the
# customer-dashboard _headers section.
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# ── Crawler artefacts ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Crawlers re-check robots + sitemaps periodically; 1h is the sweet
# spot — fast enough that a fresh sitemap propagates the same day,
# slow enough that we don't burn origin requests on every Googlebot
# visit.
/robots.txt
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/sitemap-index.xml
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/sitemap-*.xml
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

# ── Marketing pages (HTML) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# 5min in the customer's browser, 1d at the edge, 1d
# stale-while-revalidate. Means: customers see fresh-ish content (max
# 5min stale on a return visit), edge keeps a hot copy for 24h, and
# during a re-fetch the edge can serve stale-but-fresh while
# revalidating in the background. Optimised for "we deploy a few
# times a week and want fast page loads in between."
/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, s-maxage=86400, stale-while-revalidate=86400
/index.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, s-maxage=86400, stale-while-revalidate=86400

# Catch-all — SECURITY HEADERS ONLY (matches the customer-dashboard
# pattern). ⚠️ Deliberately NO Cache-Control here: CF Pages does not give
# earlier, more-specific rules precedence — a Cache-Control on `/*` merges
# into EVERY response, so the immutable asset tiers above never took
# effect (measured 2026-07-04: /_astro/* hashed assets, fonts, and og
# cards all served browser max-age=14400 instead of 1y; Lighthouse
# flagged the ~180 KiB font re-download). HTML pages other than `/` now
# take the zone-default browser TTL (~4h) — acceptable for a static
# marketing site whose edge cache is purged on every deploy; the
# homepage keeps its explicit 5-min rule above and inherits every
# security header from this single catch-all definition. Keeping the
# `/` block cache-only prevents Cloudflare's rule merge from emitting
# duplicate security fields on the apex response.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), camera=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
